From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:47:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 009: Bifrost transform feedback from vertex shaders
 (passthrough GS)

v6/v7 advertised transformFeedback but only captured from a geometry
shader (008). A vertex shader with xfb outputs and no geometry shader
now runs through the geometry shader emulation with a generated
passthrough geometry shader, so the 008 capture path (staging records,
panlib_xfb_scan/copy, counter buffers, pause/resume) is the only one.

- A vertex shader with usable xfb outputs is compiled in clip space
  (like one feeding a geometry shader) and keeps a compact copy of its
  nir_xfb_info in the serialized variant.
- At draw time, with no geometry shader bound, the emulation runs a
  passthrough built from the vertex shader's varying layout for the
  draw's input primitive class (points, lines, triangles, lines and
  triangles with adjacency; adjacency vertices are dropped). It is
  compiled once per class and cached on the vertex shader. A
  clip-space vertex shader drawn without its geometry shader (shader
  objects) uses the same passthrough without capture.
- The emulation also forwards the vec4 clip/cull slots of a lowered
  vertex shader to the fragment shader.
- transformFeedbackDraw on v6/v7: vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT writes a
  VkDrawIndirectCommand with a one-thread job and draws it indirectly.

Limits: gl_PointSize is not captured (reads 0) and points drawn through
the passthrough rasterize at size 1; gl_PrimitiveID in the fragment
shader counts across instances; transformFeedbackQueries stays off on
v6/v7. Build-tested only, no Bifrost device run. biblioklept

